 +75^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nA **linear pair** is a pair of adjacent angles formed when two lines intersect. The angles shown above form a linear pair.\n\nThe **linear pair postulate** states the following:\n\nIf two angles form a linear pair, then they are supplementary.\n\nThe converse is *not* true. That is, if two angles are supplementary, they do not necessarily form a linear pair.\n\nTo see why, consider the diagram shown below:\n\n![](images/29/29ff0dfefb0b535342f4e8060b37fb2404983fc150681bb02d18fa6e5b00f899.png)\n\nAlthough the angles are supplementary (the sum of their measures is $120^\\circ + 60^\\circ = 180^\\circ$), they do not form a linear pair of angles since they are not adjacent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1065 9518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ea9626ef-f56f-5668-8f47-81a9f68c9db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111922 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1039 "Ordering the Angles of a Triangle by Size Given the Sides" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "676e3d29-f6fa-5fe4-aae4-e9c0e974ee74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115310 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115310 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115310 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115310 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186495082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115310 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186495083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115310 #edb/ref 1039